BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comprehensive Lathe June 21 [Sundays 6 Week Intensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T170000
UID:ttl-10970663846081@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for those wishing to advance their skil
 ls from novice on a wood lathe. Class sizes are small so you will get a lo
 t of time on one of our multiple lathes. Projects will range from small fo
 untain pens\, progressing to bowls and platters with an emphasis on safety
 . \n\n The TTL Makerspace is a thriving community of like minded makers an
 d the perfect place to develop a foundation in shop safety and etiquette. 
 We will try to spend most of the class on the lathe with students taking t
 urns on our different machines. \n\n Schedule: \n\n Six three-hour weekly 
 classes\, Sundays 2pm to 5pm \n\n Outcomes: \n\n At the end of this course
  you will have experienced the following: \n\n \n- Complete understanding 
 of the anatomy of a lathe \n\n- Experience with a variety of turning tools
  \n\n- Use of an array of lathe accessories \n\n- Preparation of blanks \n
 \n- Use of mandrels and inserts \n\n- Experience with a variety of woods \
 n\n- Turning spindles \n\n- Turning bowls and platters \n\n \n \n\n Follow
 ing the course\, you’ll be able to use both Craftex and Coronet Herald l
 athes at TTLMakerspace with your active membership. And you’ll be able t
 o join the active group of Makers sharing knowledge in our Discord communi
 ty. \n\n Useful for: pens\, spindles\, bowls\, platters \n\n Want to get n
 otified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/comprehensive-lathe-june-21-sundays-6-w
 eek-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pen Wood Turning Workshop - June 14
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T170000
UID:ttl-10970629898433@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Pens have become so popular around the Makerspace that we've d
 ecided to run a workshop to teach others how to make them too! \n \n \n\n 
 \n \n \n 4 Lathes\, 4 Participants\, 3 Hours of wood-turning fun! Best of 
 all you get to take home your very own handmade wooden pen. \n \n \n\n \n 
 \n \n We will cover: \n\n \n \n \n \n- Safe operation of a lathe. \n\n- Cr
 eating a wooden pen blank. \n\n- Setting up the machine. \n\n- Turning a P
 en! \n\n \n \n \n \n Note: No woodworking experience is required. You must
  have short sleeves\, flat closed toes shoes and have long hair tied back.
  Personal safety equipment will be supplied. Pen kits may not match the pi
 ctures used for this class.
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/pen-wood-turning-workshop-june-14
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In-Depth Intro to Woodworking June 21 [Sundays - 6 week Intensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T130000
UID:ttl-10970564985025@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Description: \n\n \n Suitable for beginners\, this woodworkin
 g course is designed to teach you all that you need to get started in wood
 working by learning both traditional\, and modern techniques.\n\n Students
  will learn valuable hands-on skills working on instructor-lead projects u
 sing both hand and power tools.\n\n Projects are chosen to provide skills 
 development in a natural progression from familiarity with the unique char
 acteristics of wood\, to basic essential techniques\, to some more advance
 d topics.\n\n Materials and equipment for all projects are provided with t
 he course.\n\n \n\n Schedule : \n\n Six three-hour weekly classes\, Sunda
 ys 10am to 1pm. \n\n Outcomes : \n\n At the end of this course you will ha
 ve achieved the following goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the 
 nature and properties of wood \n\n- Proficiency with traditional woodworki
 ng techniques\n\n- Comfort working with chisels\, planes\, saws\n\n- Profi
 ciency with wood milling techniques\n\n- Comfort with safe operation of p
 ower tools\n\n- Familiarity with power planing\, joiner\, drill press\, ro
 uter and table saw \n\n- Dressing and laminating wood \n\n- Experience fo
 llowing project plans \n\n- Familiarity with joinery \n\n- Wood finishing\
 , various treatments \n\n \n  Following this course\, you'll be certified
  to use the woodshop. And you'll be able to join the growing community of 
 TTL Makers sharing knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n Certifications 
 for all courses are valid for one year from the time that they are issued\
 , and can be renewed at no cost with your active monthly membership within
  3 months of their expiry. Certification renewal requires booking with an 
 instructor\, is conducted at the makerspace\, and helps you keep your skil
 ls current. \n\nUseful for: furniture\, cabinets\, organisers\, cutting-b
 oards \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n 
 Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-intro-to-woodworking-june-21-s
 undays-6-week-intensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Leathercraft Intro - May 28 [Thursdays - 6 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T210000
UID:ttl-10970554138817@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Leatherworking at TTLMakerspace \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Learn the 
 basics of leather working at the TTL Makerspace in a small hands-on class 
 where we will study traditional as well as modern methods of working with 
 leather.\n\n \n \n \n \n Small class sizes will allow you to get the guida
 nce needed to get you making leather projects with confidence. You will ta
 ke home 4 creations of your own design and if you cant get enough in class
 \, you can use the TTL Makerspace leatherworking kits or borrow one of the
  Toronto Tool Library’s similar kits.\n\n Materials and equipment for al
 l projects are provided with the course.\n\n \n \n \n Projects: \n \n Proj
 ect 1: Leather Wallet \n Project 2: Coin Purse \n Project 3: Waterskin \n 
 Project 4: Collar/bracelet \n \n \n Materials and equipment for all projec
 ts are provided with the course. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n6 
 weeks\, Thursdays 6pm to 9pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Outcomes \n At the end of th
 e course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n  \n\n \n- A go
 od understanding of the nature and properties of leather \n\n- A solid fou
 ndation in various methods of cutting\, burnishing\, dying and finishing. 
 \n\n- Experience with stamping and engraving leather projects. \n\n- Famil
 iarity with sewing machines and their use on thinner leather. \n\n- Knowle
 dge of wet molding and the waterproofing of leather. \n\n- An understandin
 g of studs\, buckles\, rivets\, snaps and other hardware. \n\n \n \n \n \n
 \n \n Useful for: bags\, garments\, belts\, custom cases/sheaths
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-leathercraft-intro-may-28-thur
 sdays-6-week-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Game Design Comprehensive June 22 [6 weeks\, Mondays]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T210000
UID:ttl-10970549452993@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Game Design Quick-start \n\n In this course at TTLMakerspace\,
  you will go from beginner to a working knowledge of game design and devel
 opment using the open-source engine Godot. \n\n Starting with the basics o
 f the game engine\, you’ll learn how to progress from a knowledge of gam
 e mechanics to a coherent\, engaging game experience. \n\n \n \n \n Worksh
 op Schedule : \n Mondays\, 6pm to 9pm (3 hours) \n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes
  : \n \n \n \n \n At the end of this course you will have achieved the fol
 lowing goals: \n\n \n- \n A grasp of planning out fun game-play mechanics 
 \n\n- \n Familiarity with features of the Godot Game Engine \n\n- \n Pract
 ical knowledge of animation techniques \n\n- \n Application of physics for
  game-play mechanics \n\n- \n Comfort with 2D game development \n\n- \n Ab
 ility to publish and show your game \n\n- \n Working understanding of UI i
 n games \n\n \n Following this course\, you’ll be welcome to join the gr
 owing community of creators and game developers at TTLMakerspace for conti
 nued support and encouragement in your game development journey. \n\n \n \
 n \n Useful for: games\, art\, installations\, animation\, interactive exp
 eriences \n \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted?
   \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/game-design-comprehensive-june-22-6-wee
 ks-mondays
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
